  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "INTENT_COLLINEAR_WITH_IS_SCAM",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "detail": "'intent != NORMAL_CONVERSATION' reproduces is_scam for 85,602/85,602 records (100%). The intent head is therefore a scam detector with sub-classes, not an independent intent model, and its macro-F1 partly measures that easier task."
    },
    {
      "id": "NO_BENIGN_BEHAVIOUR_EXAMPLES",
      "severity": "HIGH",
      "detail": "No legitimate record carries any social-engineering behaviour. Real legitimate calls do use urgency and authority - a delivery notice, a genuine bank fraud alert. The behaviour head has never seen a benign instance of any behaviour, so it cannot learn that urgency alone is not fraud, and will likely fire on legitimate urgent calls."
    },
    {
      "id": "UNKNOWN_MEANS_UNMAPPED_SCAM",
      "severity": "MEDIUM",
      "detail": "All 25,977 UNKNOWN records are scams. In the VIVE taxonomy UNKNOWN means 'intent could not be determined', which includes benign speech; here it means 'scam genre outside the taxonomy'. A production UNKNOWN prediction therefore does not mean what the taxonomy says it means."
    }
  ]
